<article class="m2-page" id="p-aim-how-it-works" data-group="Aim" data-title="How mouse aim works" data-time="3 min">
  <header class="m2-head">
    <p class="m2-crumb">Aim</p>
    <h1>How mouse aim works</h1>
    <p class="m2-get">You'll know how the EXO turns your mouse into a thumbstick, and why your in-game settings matter.</p>
    <div class="m2-badges"><span class="x2-badge x2-badge--plain">Mouse &amp; keyboard</span><span class="m2-time">3 min</span></div>
  </header>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-aim-how-it-works--the-short-version">
    <h2>The short version</h2>
    <p>Your console only understands a controller. So the EXO watches your mouse and moves a pretend right stick for you, 1,000 times a second.</p>
    <p>The trick is knowing how far to push that stick. Every game turns a stick into camera speed in its own way. The EXO uses a model of this game's stick curve, so a mouse move turns you the same amount every time.</p>
    {%- comment -%} Aim pipeline diagram: plain inline SVG so it needs no image file. Stacked boxes so it stays readable at phone width. {%- endcomment -%}
    <figure class="m2-fig m2-fig--diagram">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 340 430" width="340" height="430" role="img" aria-labelledby="m2-aimflow-t m2-aimflow-d" style="max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0 auto">
        <title id="m2-aimflow-t">How a mouse move becomes a turn in the game</title>
        <desc id="m2-aimflow-d">A, you move the mouse. B, the EXO applies this game's curve and your Speed. C, it pushes the console's right stick. D, the game turns your view.</desc>
        <defs><marker id="m2-ah" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="5" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M0 0L10 5L0 10z" fill="#62B8FF"/></marker></defs>
        <g font-family="inherit" font-size="15" fill="#E9EEF6">
          <rect x="20" y="10" width="300" height="74" rx="14" fill="#11192A" stroke="#298DDF" stroke-width="2"/>
          <circle cx="50" cy="47" r="15" fill="#298DDF"/><text x="50" y="52" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="700" fill="#fff">A</text>
          <text x="78" y="42" font-weight="700">You move the mouse</text><text x="78" y="64" fill="#9FB0C8" font-size="13">a little or a lot, slow or fast</text>
          <line x1="170" y1="86" x2="170" y2="110" stroke="#62B8FF" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#m2-ah)"/>
          <rect x="20" y="118" width="300" height="74" rx="14" fill="#11192A" stroke="#298DDF" stroke-width="2"/>
          <circle cx="50" cy="155" r="15" fill="#298DDF"/><text x="50" y="160" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="700" fill="#fff">B</text>
          <text x="78" y="150" font-weight="700">EXO: this game's curve</text><text x="78" y="172" fill="#9FB0C8" font-size="13">plus your Speed and Smoothing</text>
          <line x1="170" y1="194" x2="170" y2="218" stroke="#62B8FF" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#m2-ah)"/>
          <rect x="20" y="226" width="300" height="74" rx="14" fill="#11192A" stroke="#298DDF" stroke-width="2"/>
          <circle cx="50" cy="263" r="15" fill="#298DDF"/><text x="50" y="268" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="700" fill="#fff">C</text>
          <text x="78" y="258" font-weight="700">Right stick push</text><text x="78" y="280" fill="#9FB0C8" font-size="13">sent to the console as a controller</text>
          <line x1="170" y1="302" x2="170" y2="326" stroke="#62B8FF" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#m2-ah)"/>
          <rect x="20" y="334" width="300" height="74" rx="14" fill="#11192A" stroke="#298DDF" stroke-width="2"/>
          <circle cx="50" cy="371" r="15" fill="#298DDF"/><text x="50" y="376" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="700" fill="#fff">D</text>
          <text x="78" y="366" font-weight="700">The game turns your view</text><text x="78" y="388" fill="#9FB0C8" font-size="13">by the amount your hand asked for</text>
        </g>
      </svg>
      <figcaption>Figure AIM-HW.1 — From your hand to the screen</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-aim-how-it-works--cm-360">
    <h2>What cm/360 means</h2>
    <p><b>cm/360</b> is how far your mouse travels for one full turn in the game. The app shows it under <b>Speed</b>, like <b>≈ 12.2 cm/360°</b>.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Lower number = faster.</b> At 15 cm you spin around with a short flick.</li>
      <li><b>Higher number = slower.</b> At 40 cm you need a long arm swipe, but small aim is easier.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Because it's a real distance, you can carry your feel from game to game. Pick the cm/360 you like, and the EXO works out the stick for each game.</p>
    <aside class="m2-call m2-call--tip"><p class="m2-call-label">Tip</p><p>Played on PC before? Use the same cm/360 you had there as your starting point.</p></aside>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-aim-how-it-works--why-game-settings-matter">
    <h2>Why your in-game settings must match</h2>
    <p>The game's own sensitivity, deadzone and curve sit between the EXO and your screen. The EXO's model assumes certain values for them. If yours are different, every turn comes out the wrong size.</p>
    <p>That's why each game comes with a short list of required in-game settings. Set them once, before you tune anything.</p>
    <aside class="m2-call m2-call--important"><p class="m2-call-label">Important</p><p>Set your in-game settings first. Tuning Speed with the wrong game settings just hides the problem. <a href="#p-aim-game-settings">Set your in-game settings</a></p></aside>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-aim-how-it-works--measured-curves">
    <h2>Measured and starter curves</h2>
    <p>For <b>Call of Duty: Black Ops II</b>, <b>Modern Warfare 4</b> and <b>Warzone</b>, the aim curve was measured in the game itself. Warzone uses MW4's measurement.</p>
    <p>Other shooters start from published turn-speed data, so their curve is a good starting estimate. You can measure any game yourself with <a href="#p-aim-speed-match">Aim Speed Match</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-aim-how-it-works--sync-to-game">
    <h2>Syncing to the game's frame rate</h2>
    <p>Games read the stick once per frame. The EXO can gather your mouse movement and send it in step with those frames. This makes tracking steadier. It's called <b>Sync to game</b>, and it's on (60) by default.</p>
    <p>Read more in <a href="#p-aim-smoothing-and-sync--sync-to-game">Smoothing and Sync to game</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-aim-how-it-works--next">
    <h2>Next</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Recommended:</b> <a href="#p-aim-game-settings">Set your in-game settings</a></li>
      <li><a href="#p-aim-mouse">Mouse aim settings</a></li>
      <li><a href="#p-aim-check-your-mouse">Check your mouse: DPI and polling rate</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</article>


<article class="m2-page" id="p-aim-game-settings" data-group="Aim" data-title="Set your in-game settings" data-time="4 min" data-journey="9">
  <header class="m2-head">
    <p class="m2-crumb">Aim</p>
    <h1>Set your in-game settings</h1>
    <p class="m2-get">Your game's own settings will match what the EXO expects, so your aim turns the right amount.</p>
    <div class="m2-badges"><span class="x2-badge x2-badge--plain">Mouse &amp; keyboard</span><span class="m2-time">4 min</span></div>
  </header>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-aim-game-settings--before-you-start">
    <h2>Before you start</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Your phone is paired with the EXO. <a href="#p-start-pair-your-phone">Pair your phone</a></li>
      <li>You have a mouse config for your game. <a href="#p-app-new-config">Make a new config</a></li>
      <li>The game is open on your TV, so you can change its settings menu.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-aim-game-settings--open-the-list">
    <h2>1. Open the list in the app</h2>
    <ol class="m2-steps">
      <li>On HOME, look under the config name. Tap <b>Set your in-game settings for proper aim</b> (1).</li>
      <li>The <b>Your game settings</b> sheet opens. Find <b>Set these in the game</b> (marked <b>REQUIRED</b>).</li>
    </ol>
    <p>The sheet also opens by itself the first time you open a new mouse config's settings.</p>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-cf-banner.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="534" loading="lazy"
        alt="HOME. 1: the amber banner, Set your in-game settings for proper aim.">
      <figcaption>Figure GAME-SETT.1 — HOME, the in-game settings banner</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>Set your in-game settings for proper aim</b></td><td>Opens the list of settings to set in your game.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-aim-game-settings--copy-them">
    <h2>2. Copy them into the game</h2>
    <ol class="m2-steps">
      <li>In the game, open its controller or aim settings menu.</li>
      <li>Set each row from the app's list to exactly the value shown.</li>
      <li>If the sheet shows <b>Your sensitivity</b>, pick any stick sensitivity you like in the game. Type the same number in the app.</li>
      <li>Type the field of view you play at into <b>Your in-game FOV</b>.</li>
    </ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-cf-sheet.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="1518" loading="lazy"
        alt="The Your game settings sheet, marked REQUIRED, with the rows to set in the game. 1: your stick sensitivity boxes. 2: Your in-game FOV. 3: the help button.">
      <figcaption>Figure GAME-SETT.2 — Your game settings sheet, a mouse config (MW4)</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>Your stick sensitivity</b></td><td>Type the sensitivity you set in the game (4.00 recommended).</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">2</span></td><td><b>Your in-game FOV</b></td><td>Type the field of view you play at.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">3</span></td><td><b>?</b></td><td>Why these must match the game.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
    <p>The required rows for each Ready game are on its page: <a href="#p-games-black-ops-2">Black Ops II</a> and <a href="#p-games-mw4">Modern Warfare 4</a>.</p>
    <aside class="m2-call m2-call--note"><p class="m2-call-label">Note</p><p>When the app shows <b>Recommended</b> next to a sensitivity, any value still works. The app does the math. A lower sensitivity also lowers the fastest turn the game allows.</p></aside>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-aim-game-settings--confirm">
    <h2>3. Confirm in the app</h2>
    <ol class="m2-steps">
      <li>Tap <b>I've set these</b> (2).</li>
      <li>Wait for the toast that starts with <b>Saved:</b> and lists your sensitivity and FOV.</li>
    </ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-cf-sheet-bo2.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="1339" loading="lazy"
        alt="The Your game settings sheet for Black Ops II. 1: Your in-game FOV box. 2: the I've set these button.">
      <figcaption>Figure GAME-SETT.3 — Your game settings, bottom (Black Ops II)</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>Your in-game FOV</b></td><td>Type the FOV you play at.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">2</span></td><td><b>I've set these</b></td><td>Tap once the game matches the list.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
    <p>Tapped <b>Not now</b> by mistake? The HOME reminder stays until you confirm.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-aim-game-settings--find-it-later">
    <h2>Find the list again later</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Settings</b> › <b>Advanced</b> › <b>Translation</b> › <b>Set these in the game</b>. Tap <b>Your sensitivity and FOV</b> to change your numbers.</li>
      <li><b>Settings</b> › <b>Device</b> › <b>In-game settings</b>. It reads <b>Not set</b> until you confirm the list.</li>
    </ul>
    <aside class="m2-call m2-call--warning"><p class="m2-call-label">Warning</p><p>Changed your FOV or sensitivity in the game? Change it in the app too, or your aim will turn the wrong amount.</p></aside>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-aim-game-settings--check-it-worked">
    <h2>Check it worked</h2>
    <aside class="m2-call m2-call--check"><p class="m2-call-label">Check it worked</p>
      <p>You're set when all of these are true:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><b>App:</b> HOME no longer shows <b>Set your in-game settings for proper aim</b>.</li>
        <li><b>Game:</b> a slow, steady mouse move turns your view smoothly, with no dead spot at the start.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Not seeing one? <a href="#p-help-aim-feels-wrong">Aim feels off</a></p></aside>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-aim-game-settings--next">
    <h2>Next</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Recommended:</b> <a href="#p-aim-check-your-mouse">Check your mouse: DPI and polling rate</a></li>
      <li><a href="#p-aim-mouse">Mouse aim settings</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</article>


<article class="m2-page" id="p-aim-mouse" data-group="Aim" data-title="Mouse aim settings" data-time="6 min">
  <header class="m2-head">
    <p class="m2-crumb">Aim</p>
    <h1>Mouse aim settings</h1>
    <p class="m2-get">Every mouse aim setting, what it does, and when to change it. Where: HOME › Settings › Aim.</p>
    <div class="m2-badges"><span class="x2-badge x2-badge--plain">Mouse &amp; keyboard</span><span class="m2-time">6 min</span></div>
  </header>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-aim-mouse--overview">
    <h2>The Aim screen</h2>
    <p>On HOME, tap <b>Settings</b> on the game picture, then <b>Aim</b>. Hip aim is your aim when not aiming down sights.</p>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'exo2-ann-aim-basic.webp' | asset_url }}" width="786" height="1704" loading="lazy" alt="The Aim screen on a mouse and keyboard config, Hip aim tab. A: Showing Mouse and Keyboard, Switch. B: Hip aim and ADS aim tabs. C: the Speed stepper at 64.2. D: about 12.2 cm per 360 degrees. E: the Smoothing carousel set to Disabled.">
      <figcaption>Figure AIM-M.1 — Aim, Hip aim tab, mouse config</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>Letter</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter">A</span></td><td><b>Showing Mouse &amp; Keyboard</b> · <b>Switch ›</b></td><td>Swaps between mouse settings and <a href="#p-aim-controller-sticks">controller stick settings</a>.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter">B</span></td><td><b>Hip aim</b> / <b>ADS aim</b></td><td>Normal aim, or aim while aiming down sights. <a href="#p-aim-hip-and-ads">Hip vs ADS</a></td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter">C</span></td><td><b>Speed</b></td><td>How fast your view turns. <a href="#p-aim-mouse--speed">Speed</a></td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter">D</span></td><td><b>≈ cm/360°</b></td><td>Mouse travel for one full turn.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter">E</span></td><td><b>Smoothing</b></td><td>Steadies shaky aim. <a href="#p-aim-mouse--smoothing">Smoothing</a></td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-aim-mouse--speed">
    <h2>Speed</h2>
    <p>Speed is your sensitivity. Tap <b>−</b> or <b>+</b>, or tap the number and type one. The cm/360 line under it updates as you go.</p>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-ma-speed.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="1128" loading="lazy"
        alt="Aim, mouse and keyboard view, Hip aim tab. 1: Showing Mouse and Keyboard, Switch. 2: Hip aim. 3: Speed 64.2, with minus and plus, about 12.2 cm per 360 under it. 4: the help button.">
      <figcaption>Figure AIM-M.2 — Settings › Aim › Hip aim, Speed</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>Switch</b></td><td>On a config with a mouse and a controller, flips between the two.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">2</span></td><td><b>Hip aim</b></td><td>Your aim when you're not aiming down sights.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">3</span></td><td><b>Speed</b></td><td>Tap − or +, or tap the number and type. The line under it is cm per 360° turn.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">4</span></td><td><b>?</b></td><td>The app's own explanation.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
    <div class="m2-table"><table class="m2-settings"><thead><tr><th>Setting</th><th>What it does</th><th>Range</th><th>Default</th><th>Start here</th><th>Raise it if…</th><th>Lower it if…</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting"><b>Speed</b> (Hip aim)</td><td data-label="What it does">How fast your view turns for a mouse move. "Higher is faster."</td><td data-label="Range">0–100, step 1 (100 ≈ 8 cm/360). Type a decimal, or up to 160.8 for faster. One step below 0 reads <b>Standard</b>.</td><td data-label="Default"><b>Standard</b> (≈ 34 cm/360)</td><td data-label="Start here">The cm/360 you like, or Standard</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">Turning around feels slow</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">You overshoot targets</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></div>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-ma-units.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="861" loading="lazy"
        alt="Global Settings, Access tab. 1: Access. 2: the Show real units switch.">
      <figcaption>Figure AIM-M.3 — Global Settings › Access › Show real units</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>Access</b></td><td>The tab with Units.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">2</span></td><td><b>Show real units</b></td><td>Switch on to see cm/360 next to Speed.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
    <aside class="m2-call m2-call--note"><p class="m2-call-label">Note</p><p>Speed only means the same thing in every game when your in-game settings match the app's list. <a href="#p-aim-game-settings">Set your in-game settings</a></p></aside>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-aim-mouse--smoothing">
    <h2>Smoothing</h2>
    <p>Smoothing steadies small shakes, but adds a little delay. Use <b>‹ ›</b> to pick a preset. Pick <b>Custom</b> to set the dials yourself.</p>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-ma-smoothing.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="1128" loading="lazy"
        alt="Hip aim, Mouse card. Smoothing shows Disabled. 1: the arrow to step through the presets.">
      <figcaption>Figure AIM-M.4 — Settings › Aim › Hip aim, Smoothing</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>Smoothing arrows</b></td><td>Step through Disabled, Light, Balanced, Heavy and Custom.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
    <div class="m2-table"><table class="m2-settings"><thead><tr><th>Preset</th><th>What it feels like (from the app)</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td data-label="Preset"><b>Disabled</b> (default)</td><td data-label="What it feels like">"Mouse movement will be unprocessed and may result in aim jitter."</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Preset"><b>Light</b></td><td data-label="What it feels like">"A little steadying, barely any delay."</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Preset"><b>Balanced</b></td><td data-label="What it feels like">"Steadier aim for a touch of delay."</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Preset"><b>Heavy</b></td><td data-label="What it feels like">"Strongest steadying — the most delay."</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Preset"><b>Custom</b></td><td data-label="What it feels like">"Tune the filter yourself with the three dials below." Choose <b>Standard</b> or <b>Classic</b>.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></div>
    <p>All the Custom dials are in <a href="#p-aim-smoothing-and-sync">Smoothing and Sync to game</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-aim-mouse--curve-and-y-scale">
    <h2>Curve, Y Scale and Invert</h2>
    <p>Tap <b>•••</b> under Smoothing to open <b>Mechanics</b>. Here you find the hip curve, Y Scale and Invert.</p>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'exo2-ann-aim-advanced.webp' | asset_url }}" width="786" height="1704" loading="lazy" alt="The Mechanics fold of Hip aim. A: the Hip curve graph, Curve Editor Mouse Hip. B: plus, minus, Straighten all and Reset view buttons. C: curve presets Linear, Ease-in, Ease-out, S-type. D: COPY and PASTE. Y Scale at 100 percent below.">
      <figcaption>Figure AIM-M.5 — Aim, Hip aim, Mechanics open</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>Letter</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter">A</span></td><td><b>Hip curve</b></td><td>Shapes turn speed against hand speed. Drag the dots.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter">B</span></td><td><b>+</b> / <b>−</b> / <b>Straighten all</b> / <b>Reset view</b></td><td>Add or remove a dot, straighten, re-centre the graph.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter">C</span></td><td><b>Linear</b> / <b>Ease-in</b> / <b>Ease-out</b> / <b>S-type</b></td><td>Ready-made curve shapes.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter">D</span></td><td><b>COPY</b> / <b>PASTE</b></td><td>Copy a curve to another page or config.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
    <div class="m2-table"><table class="m2-settings"><thead><tr><th>Setting</th><th>What it does</th><th>Range</th><th>Default</th><th>Start here</th><th>Raise it if…</th><th>Lower it if…</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting"><b>Hip curve</b></td><td data-label="What it does">How turn speed grows with hand speed.</td><td data-label="Range">Curve editor, 2–16 dots</td><td data-label="Default">Straight line</td><td data-label="Start here">Leave it straight</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">—</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">—</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting"><b>ADS curve</b> (ADS aim tab)</td><td data-label="What it does">The curve while you aim. <b>Same as hip</b> keeps one curve for both.</td><td data-label="Range"><b>Same as hip</b> / <b>Even</b> / <b>Gentle</b> / <b>Aggressive</b></td><td data-label="Default">Same as hip</td><td data-label="Start here">Same as hip</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">—</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">—</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting"><b>Y Scale</b></td><td data-label="What it does">Up-down speed compared with left-right. "100 = up-down exactly matches left-right."</td><td data-label="Range">30–200 %, step 5</td><td data-label="Default">100 %</td><td data-label="Start here">100 %</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">Looking up or down feels slow</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">Vertical aim overshoots</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting"><b>Invert</b></td><td data-label="What it does">Flips aim direction.</td><td data-label="Range"><b>Off</b> / <b>Vertical</b> / <b>Horizontal</b> / <b>Both</b></td><td data-label="Default">Off</td><td data-label="Start here">Off</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">—</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">—</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></div>
    <p>Y Scale and Invert are shared by Hip aim and ADS aim. Set them on Hip aim. How to draw a curve: <a href="#p-aim-curves">Draw your own aim curve</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-aim-mouse--advanced">
    <h2>Advanced <span class="x2-badge x2-badge--plain">Advanced</span></h2>
    <p>Tap <b>Advanced</b> next to <b>•••</b>. These fine-tune how small and slow moves feel. Most players leave them alone.</p>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-ma-advanced.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="1518" loading="lazy"
        alt="Hip aim with Advanced on. 1: Fine aim, 0 percent, with minus and plus. Below: Hip measured, and Up/down vs left/right.">
      <figcaption>Figure AIM-M.6 — Settings › Aim › Hip aim › Advanced, top</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>Fine aim</b></td><td>Makes small, slow moves count for more. Flicks stay the same. 0 = off.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-ma-feel.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="1518" loading="lazy"
        alt="The bottom of Advanced. 1: Ignore tiny movement, 0 mm per second. 2: Mouse DPI 1,000, Change in Device. 3: Feel, Snappy, Balanced or Smooth. 4: Start-up feel, 0 ms.">
      <figcaption>Figure AIM-M.7 — Settings › Aim › Hip aim › Advanced, bottom</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>Ignore tiny movement</b></td><td>Hand movement slower than this is ignored. 0 = off.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">2</span></td><td><b>Mouse DPI</b></td><td>Set on Device. Tap to go there.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">3</span></td><td><b>Feel</b></td><td><b>Snappy</b>, <b>Balanced</b> or <b>Smooth</b>.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">4</span></td><td><b>Start-up feel</b></td><td>How gently a move starts after your hand was still. 0 = instant.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
    <div class="m2-table"><table class="m2-settings"><thead><tr><th>Setting</th><th>What it does</th><th>Range</th><th>Default</th><th>Start here</th><th>Raise it if…</th><th>Lower it if…</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting"><b>Fine aim</b></td><td data-label="What it does">"Makes small, slow mouse moves count for more. Flicks stay the same."</td><td data-label="Range">0–100 %, step 5 (0 = off)</td><td data-label="Default">0 (off)</td><td data-label="Start here">0</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">Tiny corrections feel stuck</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">Small moves feel jumpy</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting"><b>Ignore tiny movement</b></td><td data-label="What it does">Hand movement slower than this is ignored.</td><td data-label="Range">0–300 mm/s, step 1 (0 = off)</td><td data-label="Default">0 (off)</td><td data-label="Start here">0</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">The view creeps when you rest your hand</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">Slow tracking gets ignored</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting"><b>Feel</b></td><td data-label="What it does">How aim stops. "Snappy stops the instant your hand does — recommended."</td><td data-label="Range"><b>Snappy</b> / <b>Balanced</b> / <b>Smooth</b></td><td data-label="Default">Snappy</td><td data-label="Start here">Snappy</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">—</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">—</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting"><b>Start-up feel</b></td><td data-label="What it does">How gently a move starts after your hand was still.</td><td data-label="Range">0–200 ms, step 5 (0 = instant)</td><td data-label="Default">0 ms</td><td data-label="Start here">0 ms</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">Aim jerks when you start moving</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">Aim feels slow to wake up</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting"><b>Quantization</b> › <b>Magnitude</b></td><td data-label="What it does">Snaps aim speed to steps. The steps grow the faster you aim.</td><td data-label="Range">0–100 %, step 5 (0 = off)</td><td data-label="Default">0 (off)</td><td data-label="Start here">25 (the app's tip)</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">You want more snap</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">Aim feels steppy</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting"><b>Quantization</b> › <b>Angle</b></td><td data-label="What it does">Snaps aim direction to set angles, at any speed.</td><td data-label="Range">0–100 %, step 5 (0 = off)</td><td data-label="Default">0 (off)</td><td data-label="Start here">25 (the app's tip)</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">You want straighter lines</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">Diagonals feel blocked</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></div>
    <aside class="m2-call m2-call--tip"><p class="m2-call-label">Tip</p><p>Change one Advanced setting at a time, then test it in a firing range. Then you know which one helped.</p></aside>
  </section>

