</article>


<article class="m2-page" id="p-aim-curves" data-group="Aim" data-title="Draw your own aim curve" data-time="5 min">
  <header class="m2-head">
    <p class="m2-crumb">Aim</p>
    <h1>Draw your own aim curve</h1>
    <p class="m2-get">You'll shape how fast your view turns at slow and fast hand speeds.</p>
    <div class="m2-badges"><span class="x2-badge x2-badge--plain">Mouse &amp; keyboard</span><span class="x2-badge x2-badge--plain">Advanced</span><span class="m2-time">5 min</span></div>
  </header>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-aim-curves--before-you-start">
    <h2>Before you start</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Your in-game settings match the app's list. <a href="#p-aim-game-settings">Set your in-game settings</a></li>
      <li>Your Speed feels about right. <a href="#p-aim-mouse--speed">Speed</a></li>
    </ul>
    <p>The graph's bottom edge is <b>Hand speed</b>. Its side is <b>Turn speed</b>. A straight line means the game turns in step with your hand. Bend it up at the right to make flicks faster.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-aim-curves--open-the-editor">
    <h2>1. Open the curve editor</h2>
    <ol class="m2-steps">
      <li>On HOME, tap <b>Settings</b>, then <b>Aim</b>.</li>
      <li>Stay on <b>Hip aim</b>. Tap <b>•••</b> under Smoothing.</li>
      <li>Find <b>Curve Editor - Mouse : Hip</b>.</li>
    </ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'exo2-ann-aim-advanced.webp' | asset_url }}" width="786" height="1704" loading="lazy" alt="The hip curve editor. A: the curve graph with draggable dots. B: plus, minus, Straighten all and Reset view. C: presets Linear, Ease-in, Ease-out and S-type. D: COPY and PASTE.">
      <figcaption>Figure AIM-C.1 — Aim, Hip aim, curve editor</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>Letter</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter">A</span></td><td>The curve</td><td>Drag a circle to move it. The curve can only rise.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter">B</span></td><td><b>+</b> / <b>−</b> / <b>Straighten all</b> / <b>Reset view</b></td><td>Add or remove a dot, straighten every part, undo zoom.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter">C</span></td><td><b>Linear</b> / <b>Ease-in</b> / <b>Ease-out</b> / <b>S-type</b></td><td>Start from a ready-made shape.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter">D</span></td><td><b>COPY</b> / <b>PASTE</b></td><td>Move a curve between pages or configs.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-aim-curves--shape-it">
    <h2>2. Shape the curve</h2>
    <ol class="m2-steps">
      <li>Tap a preset, like <b>Ease-in</b>, to start from a shape close to what you want.</li>
      <li>Drag a circle up to make that hand speed turn faster, or down to make it slower.</li>
      <li>Need another bend? Tap <b>+</b>. It adds a dot in the middle of the selected part.</li>
      <li>To remove a dot, select it and tap <b>−</b>.</li>
      <li>Tap a small dot between two circles to make that part straight, or smooth again.</li>
    </ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-ma-curve.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="1518" loading="lazy"
        alt="Hip aim, Mouse card with the three-dot button open. 1: the three dots. 2: Hip curve help button. 3: the Curve Editor, with circles on the line.">
      <figcaption>Figure AIM-C.2 — Settings › Aim › Hip aim › ••• › Hip curve</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>•••</b></td><td>Shows the mechanics, including Hip curve.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">2</span></td><td><b>Hip curve ?</b></td><td>How the curve changes your aim.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">3</span></td><td><b>Curve Editor</b></td><td>Drag the points to shape how turn speed builds.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
    <p>Pinch to zoom in on the graph. Drag empty space to move around. <b>Reset view</b> brings back the whole graph.</p>
    <aside class="m2-call m2-call--tip"><p class="m2-call-label">Tip</p><p>Made a mess? Tap <b>Straighten all</b> or the <b>Linear</b> preset to get back to a straight line.</p></aside>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-aim-curves--copy-it">
    <h2>3. Copy it to ADS or another config (optional)</h2>
    <ol class="m2-steps">
      <li>Tap <b>COPY</b>.</li>
      <li>Open the other config's curve editor.</li>
      <li>Tap <b>PASTE</b>.</li>
    </ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-ct-custom.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="1518" loading="lazy"
        alt="A curve editor (controller config shown). 1: Custom. 2: the curve, with circles to drag. 3: Save. Below the curve: plus, minus, Straighten all, Reset view, COPY, PASTE and the presets Linear, Ease-in, Ease-out and S-type.">
      <figcaption>Figure AIM-C.3 — A curve editor, with COPY and PASTE under the curve</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>Custom</b></td><td>Shape the curve yourself.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">2</span></td><td><b>Curve</b></td><td>Drag the points.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">3</span></td><td><b>Save</b></td><td>Keeps the change on your EXO.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
    <p>On the ADS aim tab, the <b>ADS curve</b> is <b>Same as hip</b> by default, so your new hip curve is used there too.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-aim-curves--check-it-worked">
    <h2>Check it worked</h2>
    <aside class="m2-call m2-call--check"><p class="m2-call-label">Check it worked</p>
      <p>You're set when all of these are true:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><b>App:</b> the graph shows your new shape after you leave the screen and come back.</li>
        <li><b>Game:</b> in a firing range, slow tracking and fast flicks both land where you expect.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Not seeing one? <a href="#p-help-aim-feels-wrong">Aim feels off</a></p></aside>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-aim-curves--next">
    <h2>Next</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Recommended:</b> <a href="#p-aim-smoothing-and-sync">Smoothing and Sync to game</a></li>
      <li><a href="#p-aim-hip-and-ads">Hip fire vs aiming down sights</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</article>


<article class="m2-page" id="p-aim-smoothing-and-sync" data-group="Aim" data-title="Smoothing and Sync to game" data-time="5 min">
  <header class="m2-head">
    <p class="m2-crumb">Aim</p>
    <h1>Smoothing and Sync to game</h1>
    <p class="m2-get">Every smoothing dial, and how to match the EXO to your game's frame rate.</p>
    <div class="m2-badges"><span class="x2-badge x2-badge--plain">Mouse &amp; keyboard</span><span class="x2-badge x2-badge--plain">Advanced</span><span class="m2-time">5 min</span></div>
  </header>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-aim-smoothing-and-sync--presets">
    <h2>Smoothing presets</h2>
    <p>Where: <b>Settings</b> › <b>Aim</b> › <b>Smoothing</b>. Start with a preset. Go to <b>Custom</b> only if none of them feel right.</p>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-ma-smoothing.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="1128" loading="lazy"
        alt="Hip aim, Mouse card. Smoothing shows Disabled. 1: the arrow to step through the presets.">
      <figcaption>Figure AIM-SS.1 — Settings › Aim › Smoothing</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>Smoothing arrows</b></td><td>Step through the presets.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
    <div class="m2-table"><table class="m2-settings"><thead><tr><th>Preset</th><th>Feel</th><th>Use it when</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td data-label="Preset"><b>Disabled</b> (Hip default)</td><td data-label="Feel">Raw mouse movement</td><td data-label="Use it when">Your aim already feels clean</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Preset"><b>Light</b></td><td data-label="Feel">A little steadying, barely any delay</td><td data-label="Use it when">You see small jitter</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Preset"><b>Balanced</b></td><td data-label="Feel">Steadier, a touch of delay</td><td data-label="Use it when">Tracking looks shaky</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Preset"><b>Heavy</b></td><td data-label="Feel">Strongest steadying, the most delay</td><td data-label="Use it when">Long-range aim shakes a lot</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Preset"><b>Same as hip</b> (ADS default)</td><td data-label="Feel">Uses your Hip aim smoothing</td><td data-label="Use it when">You want one feel for both</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></div>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-aim-smoothing-and-sync--custom">
    <h2>Custom smoothing <span class="x2-badge x2-badge--plain">Advanced</span></h2>
    <p>Pick <b>Custom</b>, then choose a style: <b>Standard</b> or <b>Classic</b>. The app shows the added delay under the dials: "Adds about N ms of delay."</p>
    <div class="m2-table"><table class="m2-settings"><thead><tr><th>Setting</th><th>What it does</th><th>Range</th><th>Default</th><th>Start here</th><th>Raise it if…</th><th>Lower it if…</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting"><b>Precision</b> (Standard)</td><td data-label="What it does">Fine aim. Higher = smoother at low speeds, a heavier reticle.</td><td data-label="Range">0–100 %, step 0.5</td><td data-label="Default">0 %</td><td data-label="Start here">0 %</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">Slow aim jitters</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">Small aim feels heavy</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting"><b>Response</b> (Standard)</td><td data-label="What it does">Fast aim. Higher = a lighter reticle at faster speeds. Off while Precision is 0.</td><td data-label="Range">0–100 %, step 0.5</td><td data-label="Default">10 %</td><td data-label="Start here">10 %</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">Fast moves feel dragged</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">Fast moves feel twitchy</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting"><b>Easing</b> (Standard)</td><td data-label="What it does">Aim from rest. Higher = a smoother start, but slower to respond.</td><td data-label="Range">0–100 %, step 0.5</td><td data-label="Default">30 %</td><td data-label="Start here">30 %</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">Aim jerks when it starts</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">Aim feels slow to react</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting"><b>Smooth</b> (Classic)</td><td data-label="What it does">Higher = more smoothing.</td><td data-label="Range">0–100, step 0.5</td><td data-label="Default">0 (20 when you first pick Classic)</td><td data-label="Start here">20</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">Aim jitters</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">Aim feels floaty</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting"><b>Decay</b> (Classic)</td><td data-label="What it does">How much Smooth leans on past movement. Higher = older movement counts less.</td><td data-label="Range">0–20, step 0.5</td><td data-label="Default">9</td><td data-label="Start here">9 ("Usual: 9.0")</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">Aim feels floaty</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">Aim still jitters</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></div>
    <aside class="m2-call m2-call--note"><p class="m2-call-label">Note</p><p>Older setups may show a Synch row with <b>Use Sync to game</b>. Tap it: Sync to game now does that job.</p></aside>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-aim-smoothing-and-sync--sync-to-game">
    <h2>Sync to game</h2>
    <p>Sync to game sends your mouse movement in step with the game's frames. Steadier tracking, no settings to learn.</p>
    <ol class="m2-steps">
      <li>On HOME, tap <b>Settings</b>.</li>
      <li>Tap <b>Advanced</b> at the bottom, then <b>Translation</b>.</li>
      <li>Scroll to <b>Sync to game</b>. Read the hint, for example <b>this game: 120</b>.</li>
      <li>Tap the frame rate you play the game at: <b>60</b>, <b>120</b>, <b>Custom</b> or <b>Off</b>.</li>
    </ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'exo2-ann-aim-advanced-2.webp' | asset_url }}" width="786" height="1704" loading="lazy" alt="The Translation screen. A: Sync to game, this game: 120, with the choices 60, 120, Custom and Off. 60 is selected. Below it: Runs at 62.5 a second, 4 reports of your 250 Hz update rate.">
      <figcaption>Figure AIM-SS.2 — Translation, Sync to game, MW4 config</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>Letter</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody><tr><td><span class="m2-letter">A</span></td><td><b>Sync to game</b></td><td>Pick the frame rate you play at. The line under it says how often the EXO sends.</td></tr></tbody></table>
    <div class="m2-table"><table class="m2-settings"><thead><tr><th>Setting</th><th>What it does</th><th>Range</th><th>Default</th><th>Start here</th><th>Raise it if…</th><th>Lower it if…</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting"><b>Sync to game</b></td><td data-label="What it does">Matches aim updates to the game's frame rate.</td><td data-label="Range"><b>60</b> / <b>120</b> / <b>Custom</b> / <b>Off</b></td><td data-label="Default">60</td><td data-label="Start here">The app's "this game" hint</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">Your game runs at 120 fps or more</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">Your game runs at 60 fps</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting"><b>Game frame rate</b> (Custom)</td><td data-label="What it does">"How often your game reads the stick."</td><td data-label="Range">20–360 Hz, step 1</td><td data-label="Default">144 when you first pick Custom</td><td data-label="Start here">Your game's fps</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">—</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">—</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></div>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-aim-smoothing-and-sync--related">
    <h2>Related</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="#p-aim-mouse">Mouse aim settings</a></li>
      <li><a href="#p-scripts-timing">Script timing and human variation</a> (also on the Translation screen)</li>
      <li><a href="#p-help-aim-feels-wrong">Aim feels off</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</article>


