<article class="m2-page" id="p-aim-translation" data-group="Aim" data-title="Translation: keys, sticks and sync" data-time="5 min"
  data-keywords="translation keyboard movement wasd stick simulation sync to game frame rate fps run ramp diagonals turn assist script timings wait variation">
  <header class="m2-head">
    <p class="m2-crumb">Aim</p>
    <h1>Translation</h1>
    <p class="m2-get">Tune how your keys and mouse become stick movement, and sync the EXO to your game's frame rate.</p>
    <div class="m2-badges"><span class="x2-badge x2-badge--plain">Mouse &amp; keyboard</span><span class="x2-badge x2-badge--plain">Advanced</span><span class="m2-time">5 min</span></div>
  </header>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-aim-translation--open">
    <h2>1. Open Translation</h2>
    <ol class="m2-steps">
      <li>On HOME, tap <b>Settings</b>.</li>
      <li>Tap <b>Advanced</b> (1) at the bottom to open it.</li>
      <li>Tap <b>Translation</b>.</li>
    </ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-tr-find.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="1518" loading="lazy"
        alt="A config's Settings menu: Device, Aim, Mappings, AI Scripts. 1: Advanced, Translation, Script Maker and 2 more.">
      <figcaption>Figure AIM-TRAN.1 — Settings, Advanced at the bottom</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>Advanced</b></td><td>Opens Translation and the Advanced Script Maker.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-aim-translation--page">
    <h2>2. The Translation page</h2>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-tr-page.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="1518" loading="lazy"
        alt="The Translation page. 1: Left stick movement slider, 0 percent. 2: Right stick look slider, 0 percent. 3: Keyboard movement. 4: Advanced, aiming stick keys, triggers, sync to game.">
      <figcaption>Figure AIM-TRAN.2 — Settings › Advanced › Translation</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>Left stick movement</b></td><td>How WASD becomes smooth stick movement. 0% = keys jump straight to a full push.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">2</span></td><td><b>Right stick look</b></td><td>Added smoothing on the aim stick. 0% = none.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">3</span></td><td><b>Keyboard movement</b></td><td>Run ramp, diagonals and turn assist.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">4</span></td><td><b>Advanced</b></td><td>Aiming stick keys, triggers and Sync to game.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
    <p>Most players leave both sliders at 0 %. Raise <b>Left stick movement</b> a little if your character snaps from walk to run too hard.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-aim-translation--keyboard-movement">
    <h2>3. Smooth keyboard movement</h2>
    <ol class="m2-steps">
      <li>Tap <b>Keyboard movement</b> (3).</li>
      <li>Switch on <b>Smooth keyboard movement</b> (1). The settings under it appear.</li>
      <li>Set <b>Walk speed</b>, <b>Time to full run</b> and <b>Time to stop</b>.</li>
      <li>Under <b>Corners and turns</b>, pick a <b>Diagonal speed</b> and, if you like, some <b>Turn assist</b>.</li>
    </ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-tr-keys.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="1518" loading="lazy"
        alt="Keyboard Movement. 1: Smooth keyboard movement switch, on. 2: the help button. Below: Walk speed 55 percent, Time to full run 120 ms, Time to stop 80 ms, Diagonal speed Same as straight or Faster, Turn assist 0 percent.">
      <figcaption>Figure AIM-TRAN.3 — Translation › Keyboard movement</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>Smooth keyboard movement</b></td><td>On: WASD walks and runs like a real stick. Off: keys slam the stick to full.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">2</span></td><td><b>?</b></td><td>The app's own explanation.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-aim-translation--sync-to-game">
    <h2>4. Sync to game</h2>
    <ol class="m2-steps">
      <li>Open <b>Advanced</b> (1) on the Translation page.</li>
      <li>Under <b>Sync to game</b> (2), tap <b>60</b> for a 60 fps game or <b>120</b> for 120 fps.</li>
      <li>Or tap <b>Custom</b> to type any rate from 20 to 360, or <b>Off</b>.</li>
    </ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-tr-sync.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="1518" loading="lazy"
        alt="Translation, Advanced open. 1: Advanced. 2: Sync to game, this game 60, with 60, 120, Custom and Off. 3: the help button.">
      <figcaption>Figure AIM-TRAN.4 — Translation › Advanced › Sync to game</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>Advanced</b></td><td>Tap to open it.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">2</span></td><td><b>Sync to game</b></td><td>60 (the default), 120, Custom (20 to 360) or Off.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">3</span></td><td><b>?</b></td><td>The app's own explanation.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
    <p>More on why it matters: <a href="#p-aim-smoothing-and-sync--sync-to-game">Sync to game</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-aim-translation--script-timings">
    <h2>5. Script timings</h2>
    <ol class="m2-steps">
      <li>Scroll to <b>Script timings</b>.</li>
      <li>Drag <b>Wait variation</b> (1). 0 % plays every wait exactly as written.</li>
    </ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-tr-timing.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="1518" loading="lazy"
        alt="Script timings, Wait variation slider at 0 percent, with its help open: natural timing so no two runs are identical. 1: the Wait variation slider.">
      <figcaption>Figure AIM-TRAN.5 — Translation › Script timings › Wait variation</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>Wait variation</b></td><td>Adds a little random time to each Script wait. 0% = exact.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
    <p>All the timing settings: <a href="#p-scripts-timing">Script timing</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-aim-translation--check">
    <h2>Check it worked</h2>
    <aside class="m2-call m2-call--check"><p class="m2-call-label">Check it worked</p>
      <p>You're set when all of these are true:</p>
      <ul><li><b>Game:</b> pressing W builds up to a run the way you set it.</li><li><b>App:</b> Sync to game shows your game's frame rate.</li></ul>
      <p>Aim feels floaty? <a href="#p-help-aim-feels-wrong--aim-feels-floaty">My aim feels floaty</a></p></aside>
  </section>
</article>

<article class="m2-page" id="p-aim-controller-sticks" data-group="Aim" data-title="Controller sticks" data-time="6 min">
  <header class="m2-head">
    <p class="m2-crumb">Aim</p>
    <h1>Controller sticks</h1>
    <p class="m2-get">Tune your controller's sticks and triggers, or leave them exactly as the game expects.</p>
    <div class="m2-badges"><span class="x2-badge x2-badge--plain">Controller</span><span class="m2-time">6 min</span></div>
  </header>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-aim-controller-sticks--overview">
    <h2>Find the stick settings</h2>
    <ol class="m2-steps">
      <li>On HOME, tap <b>Settings</b>, then <b>Aim</b>.</li>
      <li>On a mouse config, tap <b>Switch ›</b> so it says <b>Showing Controller</b>.</li>
      <li>Pick <b>HIP</b> or <b>ADS</b>, then <b>Left stick</b> or <b>Right stick</b>.</li>
    </ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'exo2-ann-aim-advanced-3.webp' | asset_url }}" width="786" height="1704" loading="lazy" alt="Controller stick aim. A: Showing Controller, Switch. B: Left stick and Right stick tabs, Right stick selected. C: Live Stick, a circle showing the stick output and deadzone rings. Below: Speed with Sensitivity 100 and Smoothing Disabled.">
      <figcaption>Figure AIM-ST.1 — Aim, controller view, right stick</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>Letter</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter">A</span></td><td><b>Showing Controller</b> · <b>Switch ›</b></td><td>Swaps back to the mouse settings.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter">B</span></td><td><b>Left stick</b> / <b>Right stick</b></td><td>Which stick you're tuning.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter">C</span></td><td><b>Live Stick</b></td><td>Shows the stick output and deadzone rings live. Move the stick to test.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-aim-controller-sticks--modes">
    <h2>Stick modes</h2>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-ct-mode.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="1518" loading="lazy"
        alt="Aim on a controller config. 1: Response Curve, open. 2: the stick modes Native, EXO Linear and Custom, with Custom picked.">
      <figcaption>Figure AIM-ST.2 — Settings › Aim › Response Curve (controller)</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>Response Curve</b></td><td>Tap to open or close the card.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">2</span></td><td><b>Native / EXO Linear / Custom</b></td><td>Pick how the stick responds.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
    <div class="m2-table"><table class="m2-settings"><thead><tr><th>Mode</th><th>What it does (from the app)</th><th>When to use it</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td data-label="Mode"><b>Native</b></td><td data-label="What it does">"The game's own aim curve, untouched."</td><td data-label="When to use it">You like the game's normal feel.</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Mode"><b>EXO Linear</b></td><td data-label="What it does">"Every bit of stick turns the same amount; the game's own curve is removed."</td><td data-label="When to use it">You want a straight, predictable stick. Needs a measured game: "Calibrate this game first for EXO Linear."</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Mode"><b>Custom</b></td><td data-label="What it does">"Draw your own curve on this game's measured stick."</td><td data-label="When to use it">You want full control: response curve, deadzones, speed.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></div>
    <p>In Custom, <b>Response Curve</b> has the presets <b>Snappy</b>, <b>Linear</b>, <b>Precise</b> and <b>Custom</b>. You can copy a curve to the other stick and invert <b>Left / right</b> or <b>Up / down</b>.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-aim-controller-sticks--deadzones">
    <h2>Deadzones</h2>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'exo2-ann-aim-advanced-4.webp' | asset_url }}" width="786" height="1704" loading="lazy" alt="The Deadzones card. A: Inner at 8 percent. B: Outer at 0 percent. C: the Anti line, saying Anti is not needed here because Custom already clears this game's deadzone. D: Limit at 100 percent for both sticks. E: Deadzone shape, Round or Per-axis. Below: Response Curve, Triggers, Stop my aim drifting and Calibration.">
      <figcaption>Figure AIM-ST.3 — Aim, controller view, Deadzones open</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>Letter</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter">A</span></td><td><b>Inner</b></td><td>Ignores stick movement near the centre.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter">B</span></td><td><b>Outer</b></td><td>Reaches full push before the stick's edge.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter">C</span></td><td><b>Anti</b></td><td>Steps over the game's own deadzone. Shows only when it's needed.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter">D</span></td><td><b>Limit</b></td><td>Caps the biggest push, for both sticks.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter">E</span></td><td><b>Deadzone shape</b></td><td><b>Round</b> or <b>Per-axis</b>.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
    <div class="m2-table"><table class="m2-settings"><thead><tr><th>Setting</th><th>What it does</th><th>Range</th><th>Default</th><th>Start here</th><th>Raise it if…</th><th>Lower it if…</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting"><b>Inner</b></td><td data-label="What it does">Ignores small movement near the centre.</td><td data-label="Range">0–40 %</td><td data-label="Default">8 %</td><td data-label="Start here">8 %</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">Your aim drifts with no hand on the stick</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">Small moves get ignored</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting"><b>Outer</b></td><td data-label="What it does">Full push before the edge of the stick.</td><td data-label="Range">0–40 %</td><td data-label="Default">0 %</td><td data-label="Start here">0 %</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">You can't reach full speed</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">You hit full speed too soon</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting"><b>Anti</b></td><td data-label="What it does">Lifts the smallest push past the game's deadzone.</td><td data-label="Range">0–40 %</td><td data-label="Default">Off</td><td data-label="Start here">Match the game's deadzone</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">Tiny stick moves do nothing in game</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">The view creeps on its own</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting"><b>Limit</b> (both sticks)</td><td data-label="What it does">The most the stick can push.</td><td data-label="Range">10–100 %</td><td data-label="Default">100 %</td><td data-label="Start here">100 %</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">Top speed feels capped</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">You want a lower top speed</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting"><b>Deadzone shape</b></td><td data-label="What it does">Round treats all directions the same. Per-axis handles up-down and left-right apart.</td><td data-label="Range"><b>Round</b> / <b>Per-axis</b></td><td data-label="Default">Round</td><td data-label="Start here">Round</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">—</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">—</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></div>
    <aside class="m2-call m2-call--tip"><p class="m2-call-label">Tip</p><p>Aim drifts after you lowered Inner? Tap <b>Stop my aim drifting</b>. It sets Inner back to a safe value.</p></aside>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-aim-controller-sticks--speed-and-triggers">
    <h2>Speed, smoothing and triggers</h2>
    <div class="m2-table"><table class="m2-settings"><thead><tr><th>Setting</th><th>What it does</th><th>Range</th><th>Default</th><th>Start here</th><th>Raise it if…</th><th>Lower it if…</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting"><b>Sensitivity</b> (right stick) / <b>Movement speed</b> (left stick)</td><td data-label="What it does">Scales the stick. 100 = the game's normal speed.</td><td data-label="Range">10–100</td><td data-label="Default">100</td><td data-label="Start here">100</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">—</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">Aim or movement feels too fast</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting"><b>Smoothing</b> (stick)</td><td data-label="What it does">Takes shake off the stick.</td><td data-label="Range">Disabled, Light, Balanced, Heavy, Synchronous, Custom (Steadiness 0–95 %, step 5)</td><td data-label="Default">Disabled ("Your stick reaches the game unfiltered.")</td><td data-label="Start here">Disabled</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">Your stick is worn and shaky</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">Aim feels delayed</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting"><b>L2</b> / <b>R2</b> hair trigger</td><td data-label="What it does">The trigger counts as fully pulled after a short pull.</td><td data-label="Range">0–50 % (0 = Off)</td><td data-label="Default">Off</td><td data-label="Start here">Off</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">You want faster shots and aim</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">Light touches fire by accident</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting"><b>Limit</b> (triggers)</td><td data-label="What it does">The most a trigger can pull.</td><td data-label="Range">10–100 %</td><td data-label="Default">100 %</td><td data-label="Start here">100 %</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">—</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">A game needs a partial pull</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></div>
    <p>On the <b>ADS</b> tab, <b>Same as Hip</b> is on by default. Switch it off to give aiming its own stick settings.</p>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-ct-aim.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="1518" loading="lazy"
        alt="Aim on a controller config. 1: HIP tab. 2: Left stick or Right stick, right picked. 3: the Sensitivity slider at 100. 4: the help button.">
      <figcaption>Figure AIM-ST.4 — Settings › Aim, controller config</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>HIP</b></td><td>Your sticks when you're not aiming down sights.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">2</span></td><td><b>Left stick / Right stick</b></td><td>Pick the stick you're tuning.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">3</span></td><td><b>Sensitivity</b></td><td>Drag left for slower, right for faster.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">4</span></td><td><b>?</b></td><td>The app's own explanation.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-ct-triggers.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="1518" loading="lazy"
        alt="Aim, Triggers card open. 1: Triggers. 2: the R2 hair trigger slider, Off. 3: the trigger Limit slider, 100 percent.">
      <figcaption>Figure AIM-ST.5 — Settings › Aim › Triggers</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>Triggers</b></td><td>Tap to open or close the card.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">2</span></td><td><b>R2</b></td><td>Slide right so a light touch fires fully. L2 is the row above.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">3</span></td><td><b>Limit</b></td><td>The most a trigger can send.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-aim-controller-sticks--ads">
    <h2>ADS: its own stick setup</h2>
    <ol class="m2-steps">
      <li>In Aim, tap the <b>ADS</b> tab (1).</li>
      <li>Switch off <b>Same as Hip</b> (2) to give ADS its own speed, curve and deadzones.</li>
      <li>Tap <b>Choose what counts as aiming</b> (3) and pick your aim button, usually L2.</li>
    </ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-ct-ads.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="1518" loading="lazy"
        alt="Aim on a controller config, ADS tab. 1: ADS. 2: Same as Hip switch, on. 3: Choose what counts as aiming. 4: the help button.">
      <figcaption>Figure AIM-ST.6 — Settings › Aim › ADS (controller)</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>ADS</b></td><td>The settings used while you aim down sights.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">2</span></td><td><b>Same as Hip</b></td><td>On by default. Switch off for separate ADS settings.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">3</span></td><td><b>Choose what counts as aiming</b></td><td>The button that means "aiming".</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">4</span></td><td><b>?</b></td><td>The app's own explanation.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-aim-controller-sticks--calibration">
    <h2>Calibrate a PlayStation controller</h2>
    <p>A worn DualSense, DualSense Edge or DualShock 4 can drift. Calibration re-centres and re-ranges its sticks.</p>
    <ol class="m2-steps">
      <li>Plug the controller into a front USB port on the EXO with a cable.</li>
      <li>In the controller view of Aim, scroll down and tap <b>Calibration</b> (1).</li>
      <li>Tap <b>Calibrate stick center</b> and keep your hands off the sticks.</li>
      <li>Tap <b>Calibrate stick range</b> and spin both sticks round their edges.</li>
      <li>Tap <b>Save changes permanently</b> to keep the result on the controller.</li>
    </ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-ct-calib.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="1366" loading="lazy"
        alt="Aim on a controller config, lower down. 1: the Calibration button, Re-centre and re-range your controller's sticks.">
      <figcaption>Figure AIM-ST.7 — Settings › Aim › Calibration</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>Calibration</b></td><td>Opens the stick calibration screens.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
    <p>While Calibration is open, your console can't see that controller.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-aim-controller-sticks--related">
    <h2>Related</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="#p-aim-speed-match">Aim Speed Match</a> (measures a game for EXO Linear and Custom)</li>
      <li><a href="#p-controls-mappings">Remap buttons and keys</a></li>
      <li><a href="#p-help-aim-feels-wrong">Aim feels off</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</article>


<article class="m2-page" id="p-aim-check-your-mouse" data-group="Aim" data-title="Check your mouse: DPI and polling rate" data-time="5 min" data-journey="11">
  <header class="m2-head">
    <p class="m2-crumb">Aim</p>
    <h1>Check your mouse</h1>
    <p class="m2-get">The app will know your mouse's real DPI, and you'll know its polling rate is healthy.</p>
    <div class="m2-badges"><span class="x2-badge x2-badge--plain">Mouse &amp; keyboard</span><span class="m2-time">5 min</span></div>
  </header>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-aim-check-your-mouse--before-you-start">
    <h2>Before you start</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Your mouse is plugged into a front USB port (or its wireless receiver is).</li>
      <li>Your mouse config is the one playing on HOME.</li>
      <li>For a measured DPI: a ruler, a bank card, or your phone to slide the mouse along.</li>
    </ul>
    <p><b>Why it matters:</b> cm/360 is worked out from your DPI. A wrong DPI makes every speed wrong. If you never set it, the app assumes 1000.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-aim-check-your-mouse--set-dpi">
    <h2>1. Set your DPI</h2>
    <ol class="m2-steps">
      <li>On HOME, tap <b>Settings</b>, then <b>Device</b>.</li>
      <li>Scroll to <b>Mouse DPI</b>.</li>
      <li>Know your DPI? Tap a preset (<b>800</b>, <b>1600</b>, <b>3200</b>, <b>6400</b>, <b>8000</b>, <b>12000</b>) or type it in (1).</li>
      <li>Not sure? Tap <b>Measure my DPI</b> and go to step 2.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>The app recommends <b>3200</b> or higher. Lower DPI makes aim coarse.</p>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-sm-dpi.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="831" loading="lazy"
        alt="The Mouse DPI card. 1: the DPI presets, 3,200 recommended. 2: Measure my DPI. 3: Check rate (Hz).">
      <figcaption>Figure YOUR-MOUS.1 — Settings › Device › Mouse DPI</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>DPI presets</b></td><td>Tap your mouse's DPI, or type it in the box.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">2</span></td><td><b>Measure my DPI</b></td><td>The app finds it with a short guided move.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">3</span></td><td><b>Check rate (Hz)</b></td><td>Tests your mouse's polling rate.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-aim-check-your-mouse--measure-dpi">
    <h2>2. Measure your DPI (optional)</h2>
    <ol class="m2-steps">
      <li>Tap <b>Measure my DPI</b>, then <b>Automatic</b>.</li>
      <li>Logitech or Razer mouse? The EXO reads it. Tap <b>Apply</b> to use the number shown.</li>
      <li>Any other mouse: pick what you'll slide along: a 10 cm ruler, a credit card, or <b>My phone</b>.</li>
      <li>Tap <b>Start</b>, slide the mouse along its full length, then tap <b>Done</b>.</li>
      <li>Repeat when asked. Then tap <b>See the result</b>.</li>
      <li>Read "Your mouse is at about N DPI" and tap <b>Use N DPI</b>.</li>
    </ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-cf-dpi.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="1518" loading="lazy"
        alt="Mouse DPI with I don't know my DPI open: your mouse's software shows it, the box or the maker's web page, or Measure it now with your mouse plugged into the EXO. 1: the DPI presets.">
      <figcaption>Figure YOUR-MOUS.2 — I don't know my DPI: where to find it</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>DPI presets</b></td><td>Tap your DPI once you know it.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
    <aside class="m2-call m2-call--tip"><p class="m2-call-label">Tip</p><p>Slide in a straight line and keep the mouse flat. Lift it off at the end, don't drag it back.</p></aside>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-aim-check-your-mouse--check-rate">
    <h2>3. Check the polling rate</h2>
    <ol class="m2-steps">
      <li>On the Mouse DPI card, tap <b>Check rate (Hz)</b>. You can also press and hold the mouse picture on HOME.</li>
      <li>The <b>Mouse sensor test</b> opens. Tap <b>Start</b>.</li>
      <li>Move your mouse continuously in circles until it stops.</li>
      <li>Read "Your mouse is responding at about N Hz."</li>
    </ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-sm-dpi.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="831" loading="lazy"
        alt="The Mouse DPI card. 1: the DPI presets, 3,200 recommended. 2: Measure my DPI. 3: Check rate (Hz).">
      <figcaption>Figure YOUR-MOUS.3 — Settings › Device › Mouse DPI: Check rate (Hz) is 3</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>DPI presets</b></td><td>Tap your mouse's DPI, or type it in the box.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">2</span></td><td><b>Measure my DPI</b></td><td>The app finds it with a short guided move.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">3</span></td><td><b>Check rate (Hz)</b></td><td>Tests your mouse's polling rate.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
    <p>The EXO reads mice up to 1000 Hz. A faster mouse (like 8000 Hz) still works and is read at 1000 Hz.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-aim-check-your-mouse--check-it-worked">
    <h2>Check it worked</h2>
    <aside class="m2-call m2-call--check"><p class="m2-call-label">Check it worked</p>
      <p>You're set when all of these are true:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><b>App:</b> Device › Mouse DPI shows your DPI, not "not set".</li>
        <li><b>App:</b> the sensor test reports close to your mouse's set rate (for example about 1000 Hz).</li>
        <li><b>Game:</b> the cm/360 under Speed feels true when you turn a full circle.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Not seeing one? <a href="#p-help-mouse-and-keyboard">Mouse or keyboard not working right</a></p></aside>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-aim-check-your-mouse--next">
    <h2>Next</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Recommended:</b> <a href="#p-aim-mouse">Mouse aim settings</a></li>
      <li><a href="#p-aim-speed-match">Aim Speed Match</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</article>


<article class="m2-page" id="p-aim-speed-match" data-group="Aim" data-title="Aim Speed Match" data-time="10 min">
  <header class="m2-head">
    <p class="m2-crumb">Aim</p>
    <h1>Aim Speed Match</h1>
    <p class="m2-get">The EXO measures how fast your game really turns, so your cm/360 is true in that game.</p>
    <div class="m2-badges"><span class="x2-badge x2-badge--plain">Mouse &amp; keyboard</span><span class="x2-badge x2-badge--plain">Advanced</span><span class="m2-time">10 min</span></div>
  </header>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-aim-speed-match--before-you-start">
    <h2>Before you start</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Your console's HDMI goes through the EXO: console › <b>HDMI IN</b>, <b>HDMI OUT</b> › TV. <a href="#p-platforms-hdmi">Connect HDMI</a></li>
      <li>Your in-game settings match the app's list. <a href="#p-aim-game-settings">Set your in-game settings</a></li>
      <li>About 8 minutes when nobody needs the TV.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>You don't need this for Black Ops II, MW4 or Warzone: their curves are already measured. It helps most for In progress games.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-aim-speed-match--get-ready">
    <h2>1. Get the game ready</h2>
    <ol class="m2-steps">
      <li>Open a private match, alone, with nothing in your way.</li>
      <li>Stand in open space with detail all round you, not up against a wall.</li>
      <li>Take your gun out and turn aim assist off in the game.</li>
    </ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-ma-measure.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="704" loading="lazy"
        alt="The Measure this game card: open a private match or the firing range on your own, stand in an open spot, take aim assist off, then tap Start and put the controller down.">
      <figcaption>Figure SPEE-MATC.1 — Measure this game: the same set-up</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-aim-speed-match--calibrate">
    <h2>2. Run Calibrate</h2>
    <ol class="m2-steps">
      <li>In the app, open <b>Settings</b> › <b>Aim</b> › <b>Hip aim</b> and switch on <b>Advanced</b>.</li>
      <li>Tap the <b>Hip: measured</b> row (1), "reticle velocity — tap to measure". <b>Aim Speed Match</b> opens.</li>
      <li>Tap <b>Calibrate</b> (1), "measures your game's turn speed". It takes about eight minutes.</li>
      <li>Put the controller down. Don't touch the controller, mouse or keys until it finishes.</li>
    </ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-ma-match-door.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="1518" loading="lazy"
        alt="Hip aim with Advanced on. 1: the row Hip: measured, reticle velocity, tap to measure.">
      <figcaption>Figure SPEE-MATC.2 — Settings › Aim › Hip aim › Advanced</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>Hip: measured</b></td><td>Opens Aim Speed Match.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-ma-match.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="475" loading="lazy"
        alt="The Aim Speed Match screen, Reticle velocity. 1: Calibrate, measures your game's turn speed. 2: the help button.">
      <figcaption>Figure SPEE-MATC.3 — Aim Speed Match</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>Calibrate</b></td><td>Measures how fast your game turns (about eight minutes).</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">2</span></td><td><b>?</b></td><td>The app's own explanation.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
    <p>To stop early, tap <b>Stop</b>, or hold Start / Menu (or Esc) for a second.</p>
    <aside class="m2-call m2-call--note"><p class="m2-call-label">Note</p><p>Some games offer <b>Measure this game</b>, a shorter run of about two minutes with the same setup.</p></aside>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-aim-speed-match--check-it-worked">
    <h2>Check it worked</h2>
    <aside class="m2-call m2-call--check"><p class="m2-call-label">Check it worked</p>
      <p>You're set when all of these are true:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><b>App:</b> the run finishes without a stop message.</li>
        <li><b>Game:</b> moving the mouse the cm/360 shown under Speed turns you one full circle.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Not seeing one? <a href="#p-help-aim-feels-wrong">Aim feels off</a></p></aside>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-aim-speed-match--next">
    <h2>Next</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Recommended:</b> <a href="#p-aim-mouse">Mouse aim settings</a></li>
      <li><a href="#p-aim-controller-sticks">Controller sticks</a> (EXO Linear needs a measured game)</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</article>


<article class="m2-page" id="p-aim-native-kbm" data-group="Aim" data-title="Native Mouse & Keyboard" data-time="3 min">
  <header class="m2-head">
    <p class="m2-crumb">Aim</p>
    <h1>Native Mouse &amp; Keyboard</h1>
    <p class="m2-get">What the Native Mouse &amp; Keyboard config type is, and who it's for.</p>
    <div class="m2-badges"><span class="x2-badge x2-badge--plain">PC</span><span class="x2-badge x2-badge--plain">Mouse &amp; keyboard</span><span class="x2-badge x2-badge--progress">In final testing</span><span class="m2-time">3 min</span></div>
  </header>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-aim-native-kbm--what-it-is">
    <h2>What it is</h2>
    <p><b>Native Mouse &amp; Keyboard</b> is a config type for PC players. Your real mouse and keyboard reach the game as themselves, not as a controller. Scripts and gun detection can still run on top.</p>
    <aside class="m2-call m2-call--important"><p class="m2-call-label">Important</p><p>Native Mouse &amp; Keyboard is in final testing. We'll confirm it here when it's ready. Until then, use a normal mouse config.</p></aside>
    <p>It's a different feature from <a href="#p-app-passthrough">Pass-through</a>. Pass-through pauses your config for menus, chat and typing.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-aim-native-kbm--how-you-choose-it">
    <h2>How you choose it</h2>
    <p>You pick it when you make a config: <b>New config</b> › step 3 › <b>Native Mouse &amp; Keyboard</b> ("For PC players: your real mouse &amp; keyboard plus AI scripts"). You can't switch an existing config to it later.</p>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'exo2-ann-native-kbm.webp' | asset_url }}" width="786" height="1358" loading="lazy" alt="Device page of a Native Mouse and Keyboard config. A: Connection Method shows PC with a Native M and K badge. B: a red card, This profile is Native Mouse and Keyboard, chosen when it was made.">
      <figcaption>Figure AIM-N.1 — Device, Native Mouse &amp; Keyboard config</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>Letter</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter">A</span></td><td><b>PC</b> · <b>Native M&amp;K</b></td><td>The connection method of a native config.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter">B</span></td><td><b>This profile is Native Mouse &amp; Keyboard</b></td><td>Chosen when the config was made.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-aim-native-kbm--aim">
    <h2>Aim on a native config</h2>
    <p>The game handles your sensitivity, so there's no stick or curve to tune. Set sensitivity in the game's own menu. Scripts assume <b>Left click = Fire</b> and <b>Right click = Aim (ADS)</b>.</p>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'exo2-ann-native-kbm-2.webp' | asset_url }}" width="786" height="1704" loading="lazy" alt="Aim on a native config. A: the Native M and K card, Native, the game handles your sensitivity. B: Edit anyway, Scale the mouse before it reaches the game, switched off.">
      <figcaption>Figure AIM-N.2 — Aim, Native Mouse &amp; Keyboard config</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>Letter</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter">A</span></td><td><b>Native M&amp;K</b></td><td>"Native — the game handles your sensitivity."</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter">B</span></td><td><b>Edit anyway</b></td><td>Unlocks <b>Scale X</b> and <b>Scale Y</b>.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
    <div class="m2-table"><table class="m2-settings"><thead><tr><th>Setting</th><th>What it does</th><th>Range</th><th>Default</th><th>Start here</th><th>Raise it if…</th><th>Lower it if…</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting"><b>Scale X</b> / <b>Scale Y</b></td><td data-label="What it does">Scales the mouse left-right / up-down before the game sees it. "1 = untouched."</td><td data-label="Range">0.1–10, step 0.05</td><td data-label="Default">1</td><td data-label="Start here">1 (<b>Back to 1 × 1</b>)</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">You can't get fast enough in the game's menu</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">You can't get slow enough</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></div>
  </section>

